--- tensor -- host-side dense n-d tensor functions (f64, row-major).
---
--- Single source of truth for the `tensor` host-function surface: 28 ops
--- covering construction (`zeros`, `ones`, `from_list`), projection
--- (`shape`, `to_list`), algebra (`add`/`mul`/`sub`/`div`, `matmul`,
--- `conv2d`, `max_pool`, `batch_norm`), shape manipulation (`reshape`,
--- `transpose`, `concat`), and derivatives (`derive` + the seven
--- `*_backward` adjoints it resolves). A *runtime* (catopt
--- is the first consumer) composes this package by building a `HandlModule`
--- with the Rust `OpRegistry` this repo ships (`tensor_op_registry`), so
--- the `tensor.*` string callees resolve to native impls; nothing in the
--- eval engine or language data knows what a tensor is.
---
--- The tensor value is data on the `serde_json::Value` boundary —
--- `{"__tensor__": {"shape": [d, ...], "data": [x, ...], "dtype": "f64"}}`
--- — following the `{"__bytes__": ...}` tagged convention (ADR-0083 §2.1).
--- `shape` is the extent per axis, `data` the flat row-major payload whose
--- length is the product of `shape`, `dtype` the element type (only `f64`
--- for now). The tag keeps a tensor unambiguous next to user records:
--- engines with the kernel `TaggedValue::Tensor` decode it at the
--- `call_host` boundary and carry it opaquely; engines without it see a
--- plain object — the wire shape is the same either way.
---
--- All 28 functions are FFI atoms: a tensor has no literal syntax and no
--- eval-vocabulary constructor, so construction, projection, and algebra
--- cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows. The `op`/`handle` declaration
--- form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function`
--- impls in `src/ops/` provide the logic and are registered in an
--- `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native impl.
---
--- `tensor.from_list(xs)` infers the shape from nested number arrays and
--- rejects ragged input; the elementwise four (`add`/`mul`/`sub`/`div`)
--- broadcast numpy-style — trailing dims align, a `1`-dim stretches, a
--- missing leading dim counts as `1`; `tensor.matmul(a, b)` is `(m×k)·
--- (k×n)` for rank-2 operands and batched `[B, m, k] × [B, k, n]` for
--- rank-3, with the batch dim broadcasting (a rank-2 side or `B = 1`
--- repeats across the other's batches).
---
--- `conv2d` / `batch_norm` take *positional optional* trailing
--- parameters: a `null` (or a missing argument) selects the default, so
--- `conv2d(x, w, null, [2, 2])` is "no bias, stride 2×2, no padding" and
--- `batch_norm(x, g, b, m, v)` uses the default `eps = 1e-5`. Both are
--- NCHW: `conv2d` consumes `input [N, C_in, H, W]` × `weight
--- [C_out, C_in/groups, kH, kW]` (naive cross-correlation — no kernel
--- flip — with `bias?` rank-1 `[C_out]`, `stride?`/`padding?` an int or
--- `[h, w]` pair, `groups?` a positive int); `batch_norm` is the
--- eval-mode `(x − μ)/√(σ²+ε)·γ+β` per channel with rank-1 `[C]`
--- `gamma`/`beta`/`mean`/`var` parameters. `max_pool(input, kernel,
--- stride?)` is NCHW max pooling with the same int-or-pair convention
--- for `kernel`/`stride` (stride defaults to the kernel); the output
--- drops trailing partial windows (floor mode).
---
--- The shape-manipulation three re-label rather than learn semantics:
--- `reshape(t, shape)` keeps the row-major payload and requires the new
--- extents' product to equal the element count (no `-1` wildcard);
--- `transpose(t, d0, d1)` swaps two axes; `concat(xs, axis)` joins a
--- non-empty list of same-rank tensors that agree on every axis but
--- `axis`, whose extents sum.
---
--- `tensor.derive(name)` returns the qualified op name of the adjoint
--- registered for `name` (qualified or bare local), or `null` when no
--- pair exists — a *registered-pairs* table, not autodiff: a `.hnl`
--- function name gets `null` since a host `Function` sees only
--- evaluated argument values. Seven pairs so far: the elementwise four
--- and `matmul` map to `(a, b, grad_out) -> {"a", "b"}` adjoints that
--- sum broadcast dims back to each operand's shape; `conv2d` maps to
--- `conv2d_backward(input, weight, grad_out, bias?, stride?, padding?,
--- groups?) -> {"input", "weight", "bias"?}`; and `batch_norm` maps to
--- `batch_norm_backward(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, grad_out, eps?)`
--- which returns the differentiable inputs' grads `{"input": dx,
--- "gamma": dγ, "beta": dβ}` (mean/var are statistical in eval mode
--- and carry none). The `*_backward` convention: required primal args,
--- then the upstream gradient, then the primal's positional optionals.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- tensor.zeros -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 0.0.
--- tensor.ones -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 1.0.
--- tensor.from_list -- a tensor whose flat row-major data is `xs`' nested number arrays (ragged rejected).
--- tensor.to_list -- the nested number arrays for tensor `t` (inverse of from_list).
--- tensor.shape -- the extent-per-axis list of tensor `t`.
--- tensor.add -- elementwise `a + b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.add_backward -- adjoint of `add`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}` (broadcast grads sum back).
--- tensor.mul -- elementwise `a * b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.mul_backward -- adjoint of `mul`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.sub -- elementwise `a - b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.sub_backward -- adjoint of `sub`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.div -- elementwise `a / b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.div_backward -- adjoint of `div`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.matmul -- `(m×k)·(k×n)` dense matrix product; rank-3 sides batch over `B` (batch broadcasts).
--- tensor.matmul_backward -- adjoint of `matmul`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}` (`g·bᵀ`, `aᵀ·g`).
--- tensor.conv2d -- NCHW conv2d `(input, weight, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?)`.
--- tensor.conv2d_backward -- adjoint of `conv2d`: `(input, weight, grad_out, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?) -> {input, weight, bias?}`.
--- tensor.max_pool -- NCHW max pooling `(input, kernel, stride?)`; stride defaults to kernel.
--- tensor.batch_norm -- eval-mode batch norm `(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, eps?)`.
--- tensor.reshape -- `t` re-labeled under `shape` (product must equal the element count).
--- tensor.transpose -- `t` with axes `d0`/`d1` swapped.
--- tensor.concat -- `xs` joined along `axis` (same rank, other axes equal).
--- tensor.batch_norm_backward -- adjoint of `tensor.batch_norm`: `(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, grad_out, eps?) -> {input, gamma, beta}`.
--- tensor.derive -- the adjoint op name registered for `name` (qualified or bare local), or `null`.
